//   - Leeds MATH3044 Number Theory module outline, https://catalogue.leeds.ac.uk/Module/UG/MATH/3044/202627
//   Lists of named results:
//   - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_theorems (number theory entries)
//   - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_number_theory_topics
//
// Gaps filled after the comparison: cyclotomic polynomials and primes ≡ 1 (mod n), Tonelli–Shanks and
// Zolotarev (MIT 18.781), Legendre’s theorem on conics, the regular 17-gon (HW §5.8), Wolstenholme
// (HW §7.8), Jacobi’s four-square formula (HW §20.12), Sophie Germain, Beatty, normal numbers
// (HW §9.12–9.13), simultaneous approximation (HW §11.12), Vinogradov’s three-primes theorem, points on
// conics mod p. Deliberate omissions: RSA, Diffie–Hellman, factoring algorithms (crypto), fast
// exponentiation (algo-2.12), Euclid’s algorithm complexity (algo-1.7), Hilbert’s tenth problem
// (logic-6.13, toc-10.15), Poisson summation itself (sig-5.14), Möbius inversion on posets and partition
// identities (comb ch. 6 and 9), the Paley-graph construction (comb-12.19), p-adic numbers and
// Hasse–Minkowski, modular forms, cubic/biquadratic reciprocity and Stickelberger (IR ch. 9, 14).
// Items whose topic is outside the three references keep a ref to the nearest related section.
